<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">9 </span>Supplementary Materials</h2>

<section id="S9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.1 </span>Simulation Study</h3>

<div id="S9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We designed a simulation based on the Transformer Encoder <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite> to address the scenario described in Section <a href="#S3.SS5" title="3.5 Time tokens V.S. Time embeddings ‣ 3 Methods ‣ CEHR-GPT: A Scalable Multi-Task Foundation Model for Electronic Health Records" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>. To recapitulate, we consider a sequence of two events, where <math id="S9.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1},t_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1},t_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are their respective timestamps with <math id="S9.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t_{1}\leq t_{2}\leq 28" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>28</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t_{1}\leq t_{2}\leq 28</annotation></semantics></math>. We devised the following rules for constructing the output <math id="S9.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S9.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S9.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S9.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{2}-t_{1})\mod 4=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{2}-t_{1})\mod 4=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S9.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\neg x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\neg x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Else if <math id="S9.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{2}-t_{1})\mod 3=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{2}-t_{1})\mod 3=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S9.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Else if <math id="S9.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{2}-t_{1}\leq 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{2}-t_{1}\leq 7</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S9.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\text{XOR}(x_{1},x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>XOR</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\text{XOR}(x_{1},x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Else if <math id="S9.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7&lt;t_{2}-t_{1}\leq 14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7&lt;t_{2}-t_{1}\leq 14</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S9.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\text{AND}(x_{1},x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>AND</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\text{AND}(x_{1},x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Else if <math id="S9.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{2}-t_{1}&gt;14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{2}-t_{1}&gt;14</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S9.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\text{OR}(x_{1},x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>OR</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\text{OR}(x_{1},x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We generated 1,000 simulated data points using uniform sampling and constructed the corresponding output <math id="S9.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. For illustration, we used the Transformer encoder architecture to develop two models: one employing the summation strategy (<math id="S9.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Model_{sum}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Model_{sum}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the other incorporating a time token (<math id="S9.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Model_{timetoken}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Model_{timetoken}</annotation></semantics></math>) between <math id="S9.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, utilizing the time interval <math id="S9.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=t_{2}-t_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=t_{2}-t_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We configured both models with an embedding size of 16 and 2 encoder layers with a hidden size of 16 and an intermediate size of 32. All dropout rates were disabled to maintain simplicity in the model architecture. The conceptual configurations of these models are outlined as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:155.3pt;">
<table id="S9.Ex22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex22X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textit{Model with summation:}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Model with summation:</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textit{Model with summation:}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex22Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e_{x1},e_{x2},e_{t1},e_{t2}=\text{Embedding}(x_{1},x_{2},t_{1},t_{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Embedding</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e_{x1},e_{x2},e_{t1},e_{t2}=\text{Embedding}(x_{1},x_{2},t_{1},t_{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex22Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex22Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{sum}=\text{linear}(\text{Encoder}(e_{x1}+e_{t1},e_{x2}+e_{t2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Encoder</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{sum}=\text{linear}(\text{Encoder}(e_{x1}+e_{t1},e_{x2}+e_{t2}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:155.3pt;">
<table id="S9.Ex23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex23X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textit{Model with time tokens:}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Model with time tokens:</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textit{Model with time tokens:}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex23Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex23Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta t=t_{2}-t_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta t=t_{2}-t_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex23Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex23Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e_{x1},e_{x2},e_{\Delta t}=\text{Embedding}(x_{1},x_{2},\Delta t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Embedding</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e_{x1},e_{x2},e_{\Delta t}=\text{Embedding}(x_{1},x_{2},\Delta t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex23Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex23Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{timetoken}=\text{linear}(\text{Encoder}(e_{x1},e_{\Delta t},e_{x2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Encoder</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{timetoken}=\text{linear}(\text{Encoder}(e_{x1},e_{\Delta t},e_{x2}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We trained each model for 20,000 steps, utilizing a batch size of 128. To monitor convergence, we assessed the model’s performance at every 100-step interval on the entire training dataset, which consisted of 1,000 data points. As depicted in Figure <a href="#S9.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 9.1 Simulation Study ‣ 9 Supplementary Materials ‣ CEHR-GPT: A Scalable Multi-Task Foundation Model for Electronic Health Records" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, the model employing time tokens exhibited rapid convergence, achieving perfect accuracy (1.0). In contrast, the accuracy of the model using the summation strategy improved gradually over time and failed to converge even after 20,000 steps. While <math id="S9.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Model_{sum}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Model_{sum}</annotation></semantics></math> could potentially resolve the constructed function in the simulation by either extending its training duration or increasing its model size, it is clear that <math id="S9.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Model_{token}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Model_{token}</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrates greater flexibility in managing time-dependent tasks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S9.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.03643v1/figures/accuracy_comparison.jpg" id="S9.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/186;" width="286" height="186" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S9.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="S9.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The accuracy comparison between the model using the time tokens and the model summing the input embeddings and time embeddings.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S9.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">In this simulation, the transformer models utilizing the summation strategy struggled to achieve rapid convergence, raising concerns about their capability to handle the more intricate patterns observed in patient trajectories within EHR data. The practice of merely adding time embeddings to concept embeddings does not appear to be the most effective approach for modeling longitudinal EHR records. This assertion is supported by an ablation study from our previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, where the performance of the BERT model significantly deteriorated after the removal of time tokens from the patient sequences, whereas the elimination of the time embeddings had a less pronounced impact.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.2 </span>Model Training</h3>

<div id="S9.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below, we summarize the pretraining configurations used for each model. For <span id="S9.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MOTOR</span>, we adopted the optimal hyperparameters reported by the original authors <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>. For <span id="S9.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CEHR-GPT</span> and <span id="S9.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT</span>, we followed the parameter settings described in Pang <span id="S9.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">et al.</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>. All models were trained for up to 10 epochs with an early stopping criterion: training was halted if the evaluation loss did not improve by more than 0.1%. <span id="S9.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MOTOR</span> used 5% of the training data for validation, while <span id="S9.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CEHR-GPT</span> and <span id="S9.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT</span> used 10%.</p>
</div>
