</section>
<section id="S9.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.5 </span>Synthetic Dataset Evaluation</h3>

<div id="S9.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We generated a total of 3,866,432 synthetic patient sequences, enforcing a minimum sequence length of 20 tokens to ensure the usefulness of the data. Of these, 3,740,307 (96.7%) were successfully converted back to the OMOP format. Table <a href="#S9.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 9.5 Synthetic Dataset Evaluation ‣ 9 Supplementary Materials ‣ CEHR-GPT: A Scalable Multi-Task Foundation Model for Electronic Health Records" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> presents a comparison of basic summary statistics between the synthetic and real datasets. To ensure a fair comparison, all real patient sequences shorter than 20 tokens were excluded.</p>
</div>
